WEBVTT

00:00:13.556 --> 00:00:15.514
FREEMAN:
Stardate 57538.9.

00:00:15.558 --> 00:00:18.343
TheCerritos is working
alongside the USSMerced

00:00:18.387 --> 00:00:20.345
in the relocation  of an ancient generation ship,

00:00:20.389 --> 00:00:22.217
which,
due to some unknown calamity,

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.914
never reached its destination.

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:26.873
Her crew, adrift for centuries,

00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:28.875
mummified
in disabled cryo units.

00:00:28.919 --> 00:00:30.747
Their most precious cargo--

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:32.923
mysterious containers
of molecular fluid

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:35.708
which generates life
from inorganic material.

00:00:35.752 --> 00:00:38.885
We suspect they planned
to use it on a dead planet

00:00:38.929 --> 00:00:40.452
to create
a habitable environment

00:00:40.496 --> 00:00:41.801
they could call home.

00:00:41.845 --> 00:00:43.238
The Mercedis here

00:00:43.281 --> 00:00:44.978
to ensure the generation ship
is preserved

00:00:45.022 --> 00:00:46.545
during transportation,

00:00:46.589 --> 00:00:49.374
and I want everyone
to give them full support.

00:00:49.418 --> 00:00:50.984
Captain Durango
and I both served

00:00:51.028 --> 00:00:52.769
on the Illinoismany years ago,

00:00:52.812 --> 00:00:56.077
and it is a true delight to be
able to work with him again.

00:00:57.643 --> 00:00:59.254
Trouble sleeping, Ensign?

00:00:59.297 --> 00:01:01.560
No, I slept great. I mean,
maybe too good, honestly.

00:01:01.604 --> 00:01:03.562
Just distribute the PADDs.

00:01:03.606 --> 00:01:05.477
Starfleet believes
this alien vessel

00:01:05.521 --> 00:01:08.306
is equipped with unique
terraforming technology:

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.266
an elemental fluidwhich can transform inert matter

00:01:11.309 --> 00:01:13.094
into a living ecosystem.

00:01:13.137 --> 00:01:15.835
Towing it will be
a delicate procedure.

00:01:15.879 --> 00:01:18.186
Even the slightest flux
in tractor beam

00:01:18.229 --> 00:01:19.796
stabilization could damage...

00:01:21.841 --> 00:01:23.669
Oh. Oh, I am so sorry.
I'm sorry.

00:01:23.713 --> 00:01:24.931
It is just so much information.

00:01:24.975 --> 00:01:26.629
I don't know
how you guys aren't yawning.

00:01:26.672 --> 00:01:29.806
Your crew doesn'tappear to appreciate the gravity

00:01:29.849 --> 00:01:31.199
of our undertaking, Captain.

00:01:31.242 --> 00:01:32.722
I assure you, Captain,

00:01:32.765 --> 00:01:34.680
my people are the best
in the fleet.

00:01:34.724 --> 00:01:36.204
They're proficient, alert and...

00:01:36.247 --> 00:01:37.901
- Mariner!

00:01:37.944 --> 00:01:39.903
I am trying to hold it in!

00:02:53.846 --> 00:02:55.370
MARINER:
Ugh!

00:02:55.413 --> 00:02:57.023
I had to yawn, okay?
I'm sorry.

00:02:57.067 --> 00:02:59.330
That guy is super boring.
Like, "Oh, I'm boring.

00:02:59.374 --> 00:03:02.377
I love museums
and dust and old gates."

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:04.901
I know he's boring.
He's been boring for 15 years!

00:03:04.944 --> 00:03:07.208
But right now, he's telling
everyone on the Merced

00:03:07.251 --> 00:03:09.471
that I don't have the respect
of my crew.

00:03:09.514 --> 00:03:11.516
If you ever
disrespect me like that again,

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.258
I'll skip the court-martial
and blow you out the airlock.

00:03:14.302 --> 00:03:17.000
Cool.
Well, live long and prosper.

00:03:17.043 --> 00:03:20.090
Don't you give me
that sarcastic Vulcan salute!

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.527
Beckett!

00:03:22.571 --> 00:03:24.834
Captain, I have the sensor data
that you requested.

00:03:24.877 --> 00:03:26.879
Huh? Oh, right. The sensors.

00:03:26.923 --> 00:03:29.752
Ugh. I'm sorry, Jack.
It's just Ensign Mariner.

00:03:29.795 --> 00:03:32.058
Ugh. I feel like
she stays up all night

00:03:32.102 --> 00:03:34.017
coming up with new ways
to piss me off.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.628
I honestly don't know why youhaven't kicked her off the ship.

00:03:36.672 --> 00:03:38.848
But since it's not my job

00:03:38.891 --> 00:03:40.284
to question your motives...

00:03:40.328 --> 00:03:41.764
If you want to avoid conflict,

00:03:41.807 --> 00:03:43.853
why not reassign her
to all the worst jobs?

00:03:43.896 --> 00:03:46.812
That way, transferring
would be her idea, not yours.

00:03:46.856 --> 00:03:48.292
Hmm.

00:03:48.336 --> 00:03:49.772
Well, we could reassign her

00:03:49.815 --> 00:03:52.209
to all the nastiest jobs
on the ship.

00:03:52.253 --> 00:03:55.647
That way, transferring her
would be her idea, not mine.

00:03:55.691 --> 00:03:58.476
Brilliant plan.
That's why you're the captain.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.217
Assignment time!

00:04:00.261 --> 00:04:01.914
Hatchi machi!

00:04:01.958 --> 00:04:04.830
I got conference room
cleanup duty. In your face!

00:04:04.874 --> 00:04:06.702
-Last time I checked,
that was very lame.

00:04:06.745 --> 00:04:08.660
Why would you dance?
That's not a danceable job.

00:04:08.704 --> 00:04:10.445
That's where all the
senior officer action happens!

00:04:10.488 --> 00:04:12.795
Plus, they have access to betterreplicator programs than we do,

00:04:12.838 --> 00:04:14.579
and sometimes
they let you eat with them!

00:04:14.623 --> 00:04:15.711
It's, like,
basically the same food.

00:04:15.754 --> 00:04:17.234
No, it's not!

00:04:17.278 --> 00:04:18.670
They get, like,
gnocchi and fritters and...

00:04:18.714 --> 00:04:20.281
Doesn't matter.
It's good, okay?

00:04:20.324 --> 00:04:21.847
-Oh, man. I got to monitor

00:04:21.891 --> 00:04:23.849
power fluctuations
in the tractor beam?

00:04:23.893 --> 00:04:25.416
I wanted
to monitor power fluctuations

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:27.070
in the impulse relays.

00:04:27.113 --> 00:04:28.898
Rutherford! I'm about
to go watch an ascension.

00:04:28.941 --> 00:04:31.117
What? That's amazing!
What's an ascension?

00:04:31.161 --> 00:04:32.554
Some people who master the art

00:04:32.597 --> 00:04:34.425
of alien meditation
can achieve inner peace.

00:04:34.469 --> 00:04:36.079
Then they transcend
the physical realm

00:04:36.122 --> 00:04:38.386
and become a being
of pure energy.

00:04:38.429 --> 00:04:40.953
-Isn't that cool?-Oh, like a Q or a the Traveler?

00:04:40.997 --> 00:04:43.608
No! It's more like studying
so much for a test

00:04:43.652 --> 00:04:45.393
that you literally
become the test.

00:04:45.436 --> 00:04:47.743
You become everything!

00:04:47.786 --> 00:04:49.179
Damn, that is cool.

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:51.312
I can't believe I actually get
to see it in person!

00:04:51.355 --> 00:04:52.704
I wonder
if it's gonna make a sound

00:04:52.748 --> 00:04:54.924
like "vrr" or "hmm" or "whoo."

00:04:54.967 --> 00:04:57.709
I guess I'll know soon!

00:04:57.753 --> 00:05:00.799
Anyway, let's see
what I got assigned.

00:05:00.843 --> 00:05:03.628
"Turbolift lubing,
holodeck waste removal

00:05:03.672 --> 00:05:05.804
and scraping carbon
off the carbon filter"?

00:05:05.848 --> 00:05:08.285
Ooh. Those are the worst jobs
on the ship.

00:05:08.329 --> 00:05:10.374
Scraping carbon off
of slightly harder carbon?

00:05:10.418 --> 00:05:11.984
That's Klingon prison stuff.

00:05:12.028 --> 00:05:13.638
This is weird.

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:20.166
Wow.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.646
Wow.

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:23.039
Oh.

00:05:25.563 --> 00:05:27.913
As I grow closer
to decorporation,

00:05:27.957 --> 00:05:30.394
words start to lose meaning.

00:05:32.048 --> 00:05:33.528
Hey, are-are we supposed
to join in?

00:05:33.571 --> 00:05:36.052
Hmm...

00:05:36.095 --> 00:05:38.271
A tzutchian gong?!

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:43.668
-Oh.


-MAN: What's happening?

00:05:43.712 --> 00:05:45.061
-WOMAN: Is he ascending?-MAN 2: I think he's ascending.

00:05:45.104 --> 00:05:47.019
-WOMAN: He's ascending.
-Really?! No, no, no, no!

00:05:49.718 --> 00:05:52.503
-Aah!
- My sand mandala!

00:05:52.547 --> 00:05:54.679
-No, no, no, no!
-I can fix it! I can fix it!

00:05:54.723 --> 00:05:57.203
I've been laying that
for two years!

00:05:57.247 --> 00:06:00.032
It was a physical representationof my inner calm!

00:06:00.076 --> 00:06:01.382
No, no, it's gonna--
it's gonna be totally fine.

00:06:01.425 --> 00:06:02.687
Just keep ascending! Computer,

00:06:02.731 --> 00:06:05.211
colorful sand, room temperature.

00:06:05.255 --> 00:06:07.431
Well, uh... there.

00:06:07.475 --> 00:06:09.085
See? It's-it's... it's all good.

00:06:09.128 --> 00:06:12.393
We're good. We're good.
It's fine. Uh...

00:06:12.436 --> 00:06:13.698
If I had known I was going

00:06:13.742 --> 00:06:15.178
to be emptying
the holodeck biofilters,

00:06:15.221 --> 00:06:16.440
I wouldn't have had so much
for breakfast.

00:06:16.484 --> 00:06:18.050
Welp, have fun
with your terrible jobs.

00:06:18.094 --> 00:06:19.400
I got to go clean
the executive conference room

00:06:19.443 --> 00:06:21.445
and eat some lobster ravioli.
Peace.

00:06:21.489 --> 00:06:23.273
Uh, no. Uh-uh. Sorry.

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:25.710
It does not look cool
when you do it.

00:06:25.754 --> 00:06:27.930
Damn it, it does.

00:06:37.635 --> 00:06:39.420
Ugh.

00:06:41.596 --> 00:06:44.294
Computer,
emergency stop turbolift nine!

00:06:46.427 --> 00:06:47.906
Ugh!
Hey, I'm working up here!

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:49.342
SHAXS:
Sorry.

00:06:57.176 --> 00:07:00.310
Oh, this is the worst!
Oh, wait a minute.

00:07:00.353 --> 00:07:02.007
Hey, buddy, do you want
to make this interesting?

00:07:02.051 --> 00:07:04.401
How? Like, bet on who can finishtheir piece first?

00:07:04.445 --> 00:07:06.055
-Yeah.
-All right, sure. Why not?

00:07:06.098 --> 00:07:07.360
Yeah, I'll get in on that.

00:07:09.841 --> 00:07:14.542
All right! Hell yeah!

00:07:14.585 --> 00:07:18.371
Syncing tractor beams
in three, two, one.

00:07:23.464 --> 00:07:25.422
Whoa. I was wrong.
These fluctuations are great.

00:07:25.466 --> 00:07:27.511
Aw, man,
look at these amplitudes!

00:07:30.993 --> 00:07:34.475
Hi. Um, I just... I feelterrible about the... you know.

00:07:34.518 --> 00:07:36.738
Don't worry about it.
Don't talk to me.

00:07:36.781 --> 00:07:39.784
Anyway, I wentand found a Hiverian metronome,

00:07:39.828 --> 00:07:41.264
and apparently,
if you just relax

00:07:41.307 --> 00:07:42.961
and let it sync
to your biorhythm,

00:07:43.005 --> 00:07:45.790
we can get you back on trackand ascending by this afternoon!

00:07:45.834 --> 00:07:48.793
You think I can realign a decade
of spiritual enlightenment

00:07:48.837 --> 00:07:50.316
by this afternoon?!

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.796
Tomorrow morning at the latest.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.276
You just have
to find your calm. Ah!

00:07:53.319 --> 00:07:55.278
I... don't... want...

00:07:55.321 --> 00:07:57.628
your... help!

00:08:00.675 --> 00:08:02.981
Has Mariner submitted
her transfer request?

00:08:03.025 --> 00:08:05.331
I'm going to frame it.

00:08:05.375 --> 00:08:07.029
She's... having a great time.

00:08:07.072 --> 00:08:08.639
-What?!
-She's finding little ways

00:08:08.683 --> 00:08:11.468
to inject joy
into otherwise horrible tasks.

00:08:11.512 --> 00:08:12.991
Then give her worse jobs.

00:08:13.035 --> 00:08:14.515
I've got her emptying

00:08:14.558 --> 00:08:16.212
out of the holodeck's
 filter!

00:08:18.214 --> 00:08:20.390
Ugh.
People really use it for that?

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:21.870
Oh, yeah, it's mostly that.

00:08:21.913 --> 00:08:23.698
Oh, if she finds a way
to enjoy that,

00:08:23.741 --> 00:08:26.396
then what the hell are we gonnado to get her to resign?

00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:27.745
I don't know,
but there has to be

00:08:27.789 --> 00:08:29.660
something
on this ship she hates.

00:08:31.488 --> 00:08:33.708
Hmm...

00:08:33.751 --> 00:08:37.973
Ensign Mariner,report to Conference Room Five.

00:08:43.544 --> 00:08:46.198
Whoa-hoa,another conference room meeting?

00:08:46.242 --> 00:08:48.810
Shocker. You guys debating
the Prime Directive again?

00:08:48.853 --> 00:08:50.899
Pretty fascinating stuff.

00:08:50.942 --> 00:08:52.857
-What is...?

00:08:52.901 --> 00:08:54.076
No, no. No laughing.

00:08:54.119 --> 00:08:55.338
I was making fun of you,
not with you.

00:08:55.381 --> 00:08:57.601
Well, since you're one
of us now,

00:08:57.645 --> 00:09:00.256
I guess you're making fun
of yourself.

00:09:00.299 --> 00:09:01.387
What?

00:09:01.431 --> 00:09:03.955
-: No.
-Ensign Beckett Mariner,

00:09:03.999 --> 00:09:07.132
-No, no, no, no.
-I am pleased to grant you
a promotion.

00:09:07.176 --> 00:09:08.351
No!

00:09:08.394 --> 00:09:10.396
Congratulations,
LieutenantMariner.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:12.007
BOIMLER :
Lieutenant?

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:13.835
Lieu... Lieu... Lieutenant?

00:09:13.878 --> 00:09:15.576
Looking forward
to serving with you

00:09:15.619 --> 00:09:18.317
for a long, long time.

00:09:18.361 --> 00:09:20.711
Good job, Mariner.
Well earned, well earned.

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:23.888
This is real! This is real!

00:09:23.932 --> 00:09:26.151
Wow! Thanks.
I'm gonna take off.

00:09:26.195 --> 00:09:29.590
Oh, right after this
very important meeting.

00:09:29.633 --> 00:09:31.635
All right, meeting's started.

00:09:31.679 --> 00:09:33.985
We need to choose
new conference room chairs.

00:09:34.029 --> 00:09:36.509
A beige chair with a leather
strip right down the middle.

00:09:36.553 --> 00:09:38.860
T'ANA:
Hey! We all agree
that a strip of leather

00:09:38.903 --> 00:09:40.383
is too ostentatious.

00:09:40.426 --> 00:09:42.385
We did not allagree.

00:09:42.428 --> 00:09:44.517
RANSOM:
Whoa, whoa, whoa.What happened to the barstools?

00:09:44.561 --> 00:09:45.910
SHAXS:
Barstools hurt my back.

00:09:45.954 --> 00:09:47.259
BILLUPS : You're
not sitting on them right.

00:09:47.303 --> 00:09:48.434
SHAXS:
Not sitting on them right?

00:09:48.478 --> 00:09:50.436
I've killed better men for less.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:53.570
-No, you haven't.
-Well, I've threatened
to kill better men

00:09:53.614 --> 00:09:55.920
-for about the same.
-Strap in.
This will take a while.

00:09:55.964 --> 00:09:57.443
RANSOM:
Barstools are cool!

00:09:59.228 --> 00:10:00.664
RANSOM :
Lieutenant Mariner,

00:10:00.708 --> 00:10:02.361
report to command prep
for mission audit.

00:10:04.146 --> 00:10:06.452
It's a monumental find, Captain.

00:10:06.496 --> 00:10:08.454
Starfleet Command oughtto just start engraving my name

00:10:08.498 --> 00:10:10.239
-on a plaque right now.

00:10:10.282 --> 00:10:12.633
Oh, and yours, too, Durango,
of course.

00:10:12.676 --> 00:10:14.112
There. I'm done.

00:10:14.156 --> 00:10:16.071
Great work, Lieutenant.Now you get to audit the audit.

00:10:17.768 --> 00:10:19.944
RANSOM: Lieutenant Mariner,  report to the officers' lounge

00:10:19.988 --> 00:10:22.120
-for management training.
-No...

00:10:24.645 --> 00:10:26.734
♪ Oh, za-beeba-dodden,
doo-bah-dum-dow, yeah!♪

00:10:26.777 --> 00:10:29.388
And that's why being a captain
is a lot like vocal jazz--

00:10:29.432 --> 00:10:31.303
it's all about the notes
you don'tscat.

00:10:31.347 --> 00:10:34.045
Oh, no. No.

00:10:34.089 --> 00:10:36.657
Now, here to teach us aboutpromoting diverse perspectives,

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:39.137
welcome
Lieutenant Winger Bingston Jr.

00:10:39.181 --> 00:10:42.793
in his one-man show,
The United Federation

00:10:42.837 --> 00:10:44.490
of Characters.

00:10:44.534 --> 00:10:46.884
Oh, hello.
Didn't see you beam in there.

00:10:50.105 --> 00:10:52.237
RANSOM:
Lieutenant Mariner,
report to executive poker.

00:10:52.281 --> 00:10:54.675
Oh...

00:10:54.718 --> 00:10:56.285
Look alive, Mariner.

00:10:56.328 --> 00:10:59.244
This game's about to get
very interesting.

00:10:59.288 --> 00:11:00.506
Hmm.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.204
I...

00:11:03.466 --> 00:11:04.728
...fold.

00:11:10.212 --> 00:11:11.300
Fold.

00:11:13.128 --> 00:11:15.608
Hmm...

00:11:15.652 --> 00:11:16.827
She folds! You all fold!

00:11:16.871 --> 00:11:18.742
Every time you all fold!
You fold!

00:11:18.786 --> 00:11:20.439
Don't tell me what to do!

00:11:20.483 --> 00:11:21.745
I'm gonna fold.

00:11:21.789 --> 00:11:23.747
I'm all in!
Woops. I got nothin'.

00:11:23.791 --> 00:11:24.835
Guess I lose.

00:11:24.879 --> 00:11:26.010
Are you out of your mind?!

00:11:26.054 --> 00:11:27.272
We don't go all in!

00:11:27.316 --> 00:11:28.752
It's a friendly game!

00:11:28.796 --> 00:11:32.408
Oh-ho-ho... No.

00:11:32.451 --> 00:11:35.193
Here I am,
trying to help the guy ascend,

00:11:35.237 --> 00:11:37.195
and he won't even give me
a chance!

00:11:37.239 --> 00:11:39.545
I want to help him so bad
it hurts!

00:11:39.589 --> 00:11:41.547
Geez, I get that you wantto see an ascension happen, but,

00:11:41.591 --> 00:11:43.245
-like, isn't this a bit much?
-No!

00:11:43.288 --> 00:11:45.029
It's not enough!
I owe it to O'Connor.

00:11:45.073 --> 00:11:47.553
I'm just gonna have to studythe ancient ways twice as much,

00:11:47.597 --> 00:11:49.642
just frickin' blow 'em away
with spirituality.

00:11:49.686 --> 00:11:51.253
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm. I don't think
it works like that.

00:11:51.296 --> 00:11:53.037
Yeah? Well, it's gonna have to.Wish me luck!

00:11:53.081 --> 00:11:54.604
-And you can finish my lunch.
-It's okay.

00:11:54.647 --> 00:11:57.868
I don't need another lunch.
Oh! Pudding!

00:11:57.912 --> 00:12:00.741
You get your own quarters?
-Yeah. It's the worst.

00:12:00.784 --> 00:12:02.220
I'm so far away from everyone.

00:12:02.264 --> 00:12:04.788
What did you do? How did you...how did you get this?

00:12:04.832 --> 00:12:07.051
-Same thing I usually do.-But-but I go above and beyond,

00:12:07.095 --> 00:12:08.923
and you don't even try.
Why would they...?

00:12:08.966 --> 00:12:10.968
I don't get it, either, man.
Bad is good. I don't know.

00:12:11.012 --> 00:12:12.404
BILLUPS:
Lieutenant Mariner,
report to ops

00:12:12.448 --> 00:12:14.015
for review of scheduled ops.

00:12:14.058 --> 00:12:16.582
Oh, great! Ops!

00:12:16.626 --> 00:12:18.410
-Pray for me.

00:12:18.454 --> 00:12:20.021
So...

00:12:20.064 --> 00:12:23.720
they like
when you break rules, huh?

00:12:23.764 --> 00:12:25.809
Utique, saeculorum

00:12:25.853 --> 00:12:27.724
lapsu...

00:12:27.768 --> 00:12:30.292
- Don't you have work?-Oh, I'm using my vacation days.

00:12:30.335 --> 00:12:32.120
So, I realized,
if you mix and match prayers

00:12:32.163 --> 00:12:33.599
from different cultures,

00:12:33.643 --> 00:12:35.123
you can increase your chance
of ascending.

00:12:35.166 --> 00:12:36.559
We can beat the system!

00:12:36.602 --> 00:12:38.822
-Please! Just get away from me!-

00:12:38.866 --> 00:12:41.172
--These florkas are a vital part

00:12:41.216 --> 00:12:43.609
of the ascension process
for the Tamarians.

00:12:43.653 --> 00:12:45.176
Stop it!
Don't come near me anymore.

00:12:45.220 --> 00:12:46.961
You don't get to be
the hero here,

00:12:47.004 --> 00:12:49.702
-because you are the villain.

00:12:49.746 --> 00:12:52.053
-Aah!
-Just center yourself
for five minutes!

00:12:52.096 --> 00:12:54.795
:Please. I'll align your chakra.

00:12:54.838 --> 00:12:56.535
-I'll Reiki you.
-No!

00:12:56.579 --> 00:12:58.494
Got to figure out a way
to be bad.

00:12:58.537 --> 00:13:00.626
Get a promotion. Got to be bad,Boimler, got to be bad.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:02.411
WOMAN : Ensign  Boimler, report to bridge duty

00:13:02.454 --> 00:13:05.631
-at 1530.
-Oh, I'll report
to bridge duty,

00:13:05.675 --> 00:13:08.112
and they'll get
exactly what they deserve!

00:13:08.156 --> 00:13:10.114
-What?
-Uh... Oh, nothing.

00:13:10.158 --> 00:13:12.508
That was a holodeck.
Uh, Moriarty.

00:13:12.551 --> 00:13:14.162
Exactly what they deserve.

00:13:14.205 --> 00:13:15.946
Mariner. Heh.

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:17.992
Care to share a status update?

00:13:18.035 --> 00:13:20.516
I don't know. We're towing arusted old ship full of mummies?

00:13:20.559 --> 00:13:22.692
If you don't feel
like you fit in here,

00:13:22.735 --> 00:13:25.086
I could find you a post
on another ship.

00:13:25.129 --> 00:13:26.522
Mm, no, thanks.

00:13:26.565 --> 00:13:28.437
Don't forget,
all senior officers

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:30.482
are meeting up later
for Ransom's birthday.

00:13:30.526 --> 00:13:32.180
It's mandatory.

00:13:32.223 --> 00:13:35.270
He's going to sing
and play acoustic guitar...

00:13:35.313 --> 00:13:36.924
for hours.

00:13:36.967 --> 00:13:40.144
And the songs, oh-ho,
well, he wrote them!

00:13:40.188 --> 00:13:44.148
They're all about the month
he lived in Barcelona.

00:13:44.192 --> 00:13:46.020
You know, I get
what you're trying to do here,

00:13:46.063 --> 00:13:48.979
-and it is sick.
-I'm doing exactly
what I need to.

00:13:49.023 --> 00:13:50.546
It's called being a captain.

00:13:50.589 --> 00:13:52.330
No, it's called being a dick!

00:14:00.512 --> 00:14:02.688
Are we reading any vibrations
in the hull?

00:14:02.732 --> 00:14:04.299
No, sir.The transport is going smoothly.

00:14:04.342 --> 00:14:05.430
All readings are nominal.

00:14:05.474 --> 00:14:07.345
Move us closer
to the generation ship.

00:14:07.389 --> 00:14:10.348
Sir, I-I believe the Cerritos
is in a better position to...

00:14:10.392 --> 00:14:12.046
We're in charge of this mission,Lieutenant.

00:14:12.089 --> 00:14:13.656
Our positioning
should reflect that.

00:14:13.699 --> 00:14:15.440
-Take us in.
-Yes, sir.

00:14:21.098 --> 00:14:22.970
You know, there's
no peninsula more sensual

00:14:23.013 --> 00:14:25.581
-than the... Iberian.
-BARNES: Commander.

00:14:25.624 --> 00:14:27.931
The Mercedis maneuveringawfully close to our tow sector.

00:14:27.975 --> 00:14:29.411
What? Put them on-screen.

00:14:29.454 --> 00:14:32.457
Captain Durango,
you are way out of formation.

00:14:32.501 --> 00:14:35.156
I don't have to explain myself to you, Commander.

00:14:35.199 --> 00:14:38.724
The protection of this artifact is my duty. Mine!

00:14:56.351 --> 00:14:58.570
-Durango!
-Sir, I'm reading

00:14:58.614 --> 00:15:00.268
a highly carbonized
particle cloud erupting

00:15:00.311 --> 00:15:02.009
-from the generation ship.
-Terraforming emulsion

00:15:02.052 --> 00:15:05.012
has engulfed our hull!
It's transfor...

00:15:05.055 --> 00:15:07.275
It's being funneled towards us
on the tractor beam!

00:15:07.318 --> 00:15:09.277
-Evasive maneuver alpha!
-It's too late!

00:15:15.979 --> 00:15:18.199
-RANSOM: Captain,

00:15:18.242 --> 00:15:19.591
we have
a serious problem here.

00:15:19.635 --> 00:15:22.420
Terraforming fluid
is dissolving the hull.

00:15:22.464 --> 00:15:24.422
-Structural integrity is inserious jeopardy of breaking...-Here's your coffee, sir.

00:15:24.466 --> 00:15:26.772
-Woops.-Aah! Are you out of your mind?!

00:15:26.816 --> 00:15:28.600
COMPUTER: Environmental
irregularities detected.

00:15:28.644 --> 00:15:31.734
Emergency force field,
Corridor 89!

00:15:33.823 --> 00:15:35.085
Whoa, did you feel that?

00:15:35.129 --> 00:15:36.782
Humidity's up.
The pressure just dropped.

00:15:36.826 --> 00:15:39.002
-I think the air's
being modified.
-Not on my watch.

00:15:39.046 --> 00:15:41.787
This is your watch, right now.
It is literally happening now.

00:15:41.831 --> 00:15:43.441
Oh, can you not,
even for a moment...

00:15:43.485 --> 00:15:45.226
Look out!

00:15:58.500 --> 00:15:59.980
COMPUTER:
Unauthorized terraformation.

00:16:00.023 --> 00:16:01.764
Whoa!

00:16:06.987 --> 00:16:08.727
Ah!

00:16:08.771 --> 00:16:10.686
-What's happening?
-I don't know!

00:16:11.774 --> 00:16:12.818
TENDI:
No!

00:16:12.862 --> 00:16:15.125
Damn this gorgeous coral!

00:16:15.169 --> 00:16:17.127
Well, this is just great!

00:16:17.171 --> 00:16:19.869
I could have been one
with the universe right now.

00:16:19.912 --> 00:16:21.479
This is all your fault!

00:16:21.523 --> 00:16:23.655
You know what?
I'm gladyou didn't ascend,

00:16:23.699 --> 00:16:25.570
-'cause you're a jerk!
-Yeah, right.

00:16:25.614 --> 00:16:27.137
You've been obsessed
with ascending me.

00:16:27.181 --> 00:16:28.878
I don't care
about you ascending.

00:16:28.921 --> 00:16:31.054
All I really wanted was
for you to like me!

00:16:31.098 --> 00:16:32.534
Wait. Wh-What?

00:16:32.577 --> 00:16:34.840
It kills me
when someone doesn't like me.

00:16:34.884 --> 00:16:36.842
I can't sleep.It's all I think about. It feels

00:16:36.886 --> 00:16:38.192
like ants in my brain.

00:16:38.235 --> 00:16:39.932
-Yeah. No, I get that.
-Oh, please.

00:16:39.976 --> 00:16:42.109
You haven't had
a negative thought for years.

00:16:50.204 --> 00:16:52.597
Well, since we're gonna die
here, I'll just tell you.

00:16:52.641 --> 00:16:54.164
I was never going to ascend.

00:16:54.208 --> 00:16:55.644
I was faking.

00:16:55.687 --> 00:16:58.168
-What? Why?
-It's hard to stand out
in Starfleet.

00:16:58.212 --> 00:17:01.041
This gave me an edge.
It was my thing.

00:17:01.084 --> 00:17:02.738
I was the ascension guy.

00:17:02.781 --> 00:17:04.914
But then, I was going
for so long notascending

00:17:04.957 --> 00:17:07.395
that I got worried that people
would catch on, which is why

00:17:07.438 --> 00:17:08.700
I used you as cover.

00:17:08.744 --> 00:17:10.093
I'm a jerk.

00:17:10.137 --> 00:17:11.877
We're bothjerks!

00:17:11.921 --> 00:17:13.879
We wanted to be liked,
and lied about it.

00:17:13.923 --> 00:17:15.490
I think that means
we're best friends!

00:17:15.533 --> 00:17:18.841
I'm about to die
with my best friend!

00:17:20.451 --> 00:17:22.497
If we can get down
to the environmental controls,

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:24.847
-there might be a way
to reverse this.
-Uh... mm.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:26.805
Are you sure
that's the best rock for this?

00:17:26.849 --> 00:17:28.981
What? Yes. No.
Yes, it's fine. It's a rock.

00:17:29.025 --> 00:17:30.635
Look, I'm-I'm just saying,

00:17:30.679 --> 00:17:32.550
I think you should use
the shale over there.

00:17:32.594 --> 00:17:35.075
Mom, it is the same thing.
Just leave me alone.

00:17:35.118 --> 00:17:37.338
It's just maybe you'd want one
with more of a point.

00:17:37.381 --> 00:17:38.556
Oh, my God! Why do you

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:40.602
have to second-guess every
choice I make?

00:17:40.645 --> 00:17:42.604
...suggestion to help you,
Beckett. What-what

00:17:42.647 --> 00:17:43.996
-am I supposed to do?
-Right?

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.042
Just stand by and let you keep
making a mistake?

00:17:46.086 --> 00:17:49.132
What I would prefer isif you would just let me do me.

00:17:49.176 --> 00:17:51.047
There. See?

00:17:51.091 --> 00:17:52.614
The rock was fine.

00:17:52.657 --> 00:17:54.790
Yeah, well, we could have
gotten here faster.

00:17:56.705 --> 00:17:58.620
-You're going a little fast,
don't you think?
-Yup.

00:17:58.663 --> 00:18:00.230
-I thought you wanted fast.
-Not that fast.

00:18:00.274 --> 00:18:02.014
Are you trying
to get us killed here?

00:18:02.058 --> 00:18:05.061
Make sureyou're gripping with both hands.

00:18:05.105 --> 00:18:07.368
You know, okay, okay,
you know what?

00:18:07.411 --> 00:18:08.673
-Maybe I should just lead.
-Oh, my God!

00:18:08.717 --> 00:18:10.458
Will you just stop?!

00:18:10.501 --> 00:18:12.764
I am good at this.
Just trust me!

00:18:12.808 --> 00:18:14.592
-Well, I'm just
looking out for you.
-Yeah.

00:18:14.636 --> 00:18:17.247
That's the whole problem, Mom.
You treat me like a child.

00:18:17.291 --> 00:18:19.728
Well, if you would stop acting
like a child

00:18:19.771 --> 00:18:21.643
and more like
a mature crew member,

00:18:21.686 --> 00:18:22.992
then I would treat you
accordingly.

00:18:23.035 --> 00:18:24.602
Oh, you think I'm immature?

00:18:24.646 --> 00:18:26.561
You're the one trying
to trick me into quitting.

00:18:26.604 --> 00:18:28.302
How is that mature?

00:18:28.345 --> 00:18:30.739
Yeah, that's what I thought,
Carol.

00:18:30.782 --> 00:18:32.567
You did not
just call me "Carol."

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:34.264
Whatever, Carol.

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:43.273
Oh, no, this is it!

00:18:59.681 --> 00:19:02.162
-Ah.

00:19:03.554 --> 00:19:05.339
No!

00:19:05.382 --> 00:19:07.428
- Aah! No!

00:19:09.343 --> 00:19:10.866
Get out of here!

00:19:10.909 --> 00:19:13.434
I'll be okay.
You need to save yourself.

00:19:13.477 --> 00:19:15.087
No way.
I'm not leaving you!

00:19:15.131 --> 00:19:16.959
Tendi, it's okay.

00:19:17.002 --> 00:19:18.700
I did this for you.

00:19:18.743 --> 00:19:21.181
No!

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:25.010
Yes! The systems
are still on line.

00:19:25.054 --> 00:19:27.926
Affected areas are saturated
with carbon polymer dust.

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:30.581
We need Parizene gas. Flood theship, then trigger a reversion

00:19:30.625 --> 00:19:32.540
with radiation
from the main deflector.

00:19:32.583 --> 00:19:34.933
Unless you think
we should use a pointier rock.

00:19:34.977 --> 00:19:38.415
No, that's... exactly what
I was going to suggest.

00:19:38.459 --> 00:19:39.851
I'm just impressed.

00:19:39.895 --> 00:19:41.853
You read my mission brief,
didn't you?

00:19:41.897 --> 00:19:44.029
No. I... No.
Well, I mean, maybe a little,

00:19:44.073 --> 00:19:46.423
but just ironically,just so I could make fun of it.

00:19:46.467 --> 00:19:48.817
Uh-huh. Okay.
Computer, hit it.

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:50.210
COMPUTER:
Hitting it.

00:20:00.916 --> 00:20:03.179
Oh, my gosh.
We're gonna be okay!

00:20:03.223 --> 00:20:05.355
Holy .
I was so ready to die.

00:20:05.399 --> 00:20:06.878
You saved my life.

00:20:06.922 --> 00:20:08.358
You saved mine first.

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:13.581
-Oh, no. What's happening?!

00:20:13.624 --> 00:20:15.409
-Oh, my gosh, you're ascending!-

00:20:15.452 --> 00:20:17.193
I am? I am!

00:20:17.237 --> 00:20:18.716
-Oh. Ah!
-It must have been
when you saved me!

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:20.152
When you were willing
to sacrifice yourself for me!

00:20:20.196 --> 00:20:21.719
I pretended to be finding myself

00:20:21.763 --> 00:20:24.374
for so long,
I guess I actually did!

00:20:24.418 --> 00:20:25.897
I... Ow. Ooh, okay. Wow.

00:20:25.941 --> 00:20:27.290
Oh, that actually burns.

00:20:27.334 --> 00:20:28.813
Uh, is this supposed
to be happening?

00:20:28.857 --> 00:20:30.511
-Uh-oh. Okay, you're smoking.
-It burns.

00:20:30.554 --> 00:20:32.034
It burns! Aah! Help!

00:20:32.077 --> 00:20:33.514
Oh, I don't...
I don't want to ascend!

00:20:33.557 --> 00:20:35.342
-Drop and roll!

00:20:35.385 --> 00:20:37.909
Drop and roll! Drop back
into the physical and roll.

00:20:37.953 --> 00:20:39.476
-Drop back into the physical
and roll!
-Aah!

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:40.912
Time has no meaning!

00:20:40.956 --> 00:20:42.305
Aah! No, it's happening!

00:20:42.349 --> 00:20:44.133
I'm everywhere and nowhere!

00:20:44.176 --> 00:20:46.309
I can see everything!

00:20:46.353 --> 00:20:48.746
I'm turning into pure energy!

00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:50.618
-Why is it taking so long?!
-Aah!

00:20:50.661 --> 00:20:52.924
Aah! I see Abraham Lincoln!

00:20:52.968 --> 00:20:56.406
The universe is balanced
on the back of a giant koala!

00:20:56.450 --> 00:20:59.583
Why is he smiling?
What does he know?

00:20:59.627 --> 00:21:02.891
The secret... of... life is...

00:21:07.548 --> 00:21:11.247
Uh, all right. Well, good luck
being everything.

00:21:11.291 --> 00:21:13.118
Sorry I helped.

00:21:13.162 --> 00:21:15.295
-Ransom, report.
-All systems stable, Captain.

00:21:15.338 --> 00:21:17.297
But theMerced--
she had far greater exposure

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:18.559
to the terraform cloud.

00:21:18.602 --> 00:21:20.561
Her life support's critical.

00:21:20.604 --> 00:21:22.519
Oh, man. At-at this point,
they need a whole new ship.

00:21:22.563 --> 00:21:24.956
Or... a whole old one.

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:27.394
Initiating emergency transport
for all crew

00:21:27.437 --> 00:21:29.221
of the Merced
to the generation ship.

00:21:29.265 --> 00:21:30.745
Beam them
into the stasis chamber.

00:21:30.788 --> 00:21:33.095
It's still sealed off
and should be safe.

00:21:33.138 --> 00:21:34.705
Huh. Durango should be
right at home

00:21:34.749 --> 00:21:36.968
with some dusty old mummies.

00:21:45.629 --> 00:21:47.327
Oh, my gosh, we did it.
We did it!

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:49.329
All crew accounted for!

00:22:03.125 --> 00:22:05.301
RANSOM:
Captain Freeman,  Admiral Vassery is on his way.

00:22:05.345 --> 00:22:06.650
Very good.

00:22:06.694 --> 00:22:08.609
I'm really gladwe found a way to work together.

00:22:08.652 --> 00:22:10.001
Yeah, you know,
it's a nice change of pace.

00:22:10.045 --> 00:22:11.394
Going for each other's jugulars

00:22:11.438 --> 00:22:12.787
all the time is
kind of exhausting.

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:15.920
-I'm proud of you.
-Oh. Thanks, Mom.

00:22:15.964 --> 00:22:18.358
Maybe you arefit to be one
of my senior officers.

00:22:18.401 --> 00:22:22.492
Your chair right next to mine,spending all our time together,

00:22:22.536 --> 00:22:24.668
an unstoppable
mommy-daughter team!

00:22:26.409 --> 00:22:29.194
Admiral Vassery,
welcome to the Cerritos.

00:22:29.238 --> 00:22:32.546
Starfleet commends your braveryand ingenuity.

00:22:32.589 --> 00:22:35.375
Now if you'll excuse me,
I have to get back to work.

00:22:35.418 --> 00:22:37.028
Apparently, we've picked up
a strange signal

00:22:37.072 --> 00:22:38.378
on our sense-oars.

00:22:38.421 --> 00:22:39.901
Quite all right, Admiral.

00:22:39.944 --> 00:22:41.685
And what did
your sense-oarsshow?

00:22:41.729 --> 00:22:44.209
Well, nothing at first,
but the long-range

00:22:44.253 --> 00:22:45.689
-sense-oars revealed...
-Whoa. Whoa.

00:22:45.733 --> 00:22:47.517
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa. I am sorry.

00:22:47.561 --> 00:22:50.085
Are you trying to say the word
"sensors," 'cause to me,

00:22:50.128 --> 00:22:52.043
you're saying "sense-oars."
What is that?

00:22:52.087 --> 00:22:54.132
That's how it's said.
"Sense-oars."

00:22:54.176 --> 00:22:57.222
-Everyone knows that.
-Sense-oars. Sense-oars.

00:22:57.266 --> 00:22:58.528
Yes, that's right.
It sounds right to me.

00:22:58.572 --> 00:23:00.051
Me, too.
I say it like that.

00:23:00.095 --> 00:23:01.705
What? No, you don't.
This is nuts.

00:23:01.749 --> 00:23:03.228
Yo, she's making fun of you,
dummy.

00:23:03.272 --> 00:23:04.708
She doesn't say "sense-oars."

00:23:04.752 --> 00:23:06.536
Well, of course I do.
: Stop it.

00:23:06.580 --> 00:23:08.451
Is this
how your crew treats authority

00:23:08.495 --> 00:23:10.540
when it's known
I mispronounce things?

00:23:10.584 --> 00:23:12.150
Are you really
making fawnof me?

00:23:12.194 --> 00:23:13.543
Admiral, no.

00:23:13.587 --> 00:23:15.327
I thought we came
to an understanding.

00:23:15.371 --> 00:23:17.417
Uh, maybe you need
to adjust your "sense-oars."

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:18.853
Would you just stop?

00:23:18.896 --> 00:23:21.029
I have never been shown
such disrespect and...

00:23:21.072 --> 00:23:23.466
-Is she yawning?!

00:23:23.510 --> 00:23:25.294
You know,
when O'Connor was screaming

00:23:25.337 --> 00:23:27.296
and turning into energy,
it made me realize

00:23:27.339 --> 00:23:29.341
that life's too short
to be hung up

00:23:29.385 --> 00:23:31.343
on whether everyone
on the ship likes me.

00:23:31.387 --> 00:23:33.476
That's great, 'cause I'm sure
there's at least a few

00:23:33.520 --> 00:23:34.912
-who don't.

00:23:34.956 --> 00:23:37.132
And who cares? Not me.

00:23:37.175 --> 00:23:38.916
So, who are these few people?
What did they say?

00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:40.657
Do they not like me?
You know what? I don't care.

00:23:40.701 --> 00:23:42.224
But if someone said something,
I feel like I should know.

00:23:42.267 --> 00:23:43.312
Who was it?!

00:23:43.355 --> 00:23:45.401
Where's your pip?

00:23:45.445 --> 00:23:47.490
Uh, I'm pretty good
at getting demoted.

00:23:47.534 --> 00:23:49.013
In the last hour?!

00:23:49.057 --> 00:23:50.493
Uh, yeah. Apparently,
the captain doesn't like

00:23:50.537 --> 00:23:52.190
looking stupid
in front of an admiral, so...

00:23:52.234 --> 00:23:53.801
What I... But I-I can't.

